The change is now committed. The improvement replaces silent error swallowing (let _ = ...) in the update rollback path with proper error reporting:

• Before: If the update failed and the backup restore also failed, both errors were silently discarded with let _ = .... The user would see "Failed to extract archive" but wouldn't know their binary might be corrupted and a backup exists.

• After: If the backup restore fails, the user gets a CRITICAL warning with the exact backup path so they can manually recover. If the restore succeeds, the backup is cleaned up as before.
